module tasks.`2026-11-21-full-suite-last-two`

task FullSuiteLastTwo {
  title "Full make test-parity: Dream C1 pinned producer key order, and acp_face max_tokens ending observed as null"
  verify $ make test-parity
  paths "crates/bbt-proto", "crates/bboxy450-harness", "crates/bbt-mux", "scripts", "verification"
  brief """
    Our stand: fix the cause; never loosen an assertion or re-pin bytes to hide a regression.

    ## Failure 1 (inherited, reproduced on clean 21e8baacd)
    `bboxy450-term-proto::dream_c1 public_controls_and_pages_conform_to_pinned_producer_schema_and_bytes`: `inspect` emits keys `method,v,op_id,sources`, the pinned producer bytes order them differently. Repro: `sh scripts/quarantine-test.sh --workspace --exclude bboxy450-harness --locked --test dream_c1 -E 'package(bboxy450-term-proto) & test(=public_controls_and_pages_conform_to_pinned_producer_schema_and_bytes)'`. Suspect: workspace-wide `serde_json/preserve_order` (harness d63534e, pinned since ui-kit f17cc5295) changed serialization of a struct/map the pin expects canonical (sorted) or producer-ordered. Fix by making the producer's wire order explicit where it is serialized (as ce7bcfe33 did with the canonical C1 writer), not by re-pinning bytes, unless you prove the producer itself legitimately changed.

    ## Failure 2 (seen on the old pin; recheck on current pin `6bf5c2c4`+)
    `bboxy450-harness::acp_face max_tokens_max_rounds_and_error_replies_match_the_ending` expects `max_tokens`, observes `null` at `crates/bboxy450-harness/tests/acp_face.rs:311`. Suspect: the Interrupt catalogue (harness `src/interrupt.rs`, `c50a9767`/`8d8a1c34`) now routes MaxTokens through an interrupt cause and the face no longer reports the ending. The ending must stay visible (`context.max_tokens` is a cause, not a replacement for the stop reason). Fix in the harness, land through harness main, `make bump-harness`.

    ## Rules
    Run long commands detached (`nohup ... &`, exit codes under `target/suite-handoff/`), poll briefly. One full gate machine-wide (`pgrep -fl ci-local.sh`). Report with `make test-parity` as `verify_result.command`.

    ## Report from seat:01M7ZVK9YFPRSBR7EJF6DPC5E1

    Dream C1 corpus 3/3 and ACP face 19/19 passed. Harness main carries 9dc1cb4 and bd4893b, the latter removing a stale loader image comparison that blocked workspace clippy. The wire fix removes dependence on serde_json map order. The ACP fix preserves the recovery causes and restores the two stop reasons. Candidate 1e23b5207 passed build and clippy, then make test-parity exited 2 on MUX shutdown timing and a Git temporary-file EINVAL (2,895/2,897 passed). Both tests passed serially on the same candidate. Term is clean and unpushed. Unblock by assigning the two parallel MUX gate failures for investigation.

