            "reference": "/Users/feral/mydev/bbx-gate-repairs/target/suite-handoff/mux-isolated.log"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
    ```

    ## Oracle ruling, 2026-11-21 17:40: land the candidate
    - The two target failures are fixed (Dream C1 corpus 3/3, ACP face 19/19; harness `9dc1cb40`, `bd4893b3` on harness main). The remaining `make test-parity` failures, `logic::ownership_tests::projection_ownership_real_io_survives_cancel_restart_and_root_aba` (shutdown timing) and `provenance::twenty_commit_rebase_keeps_control_requests_responsive` (Git temporary file EINVAL), pass serially on the same candidate and the provenance one already flaked on unrelated code on 2026-11-20. They are parallel-run test-isolation flakes, moved to [[tasks/2026-11-21-parallel-run-flakes]].
    - **Do:** rebase `1e23b5207`/`f3dfb3414` onto origin/main and `make land` (detached, one gate machine-wide). Report with `make test-parity` as the command, its real exit (2), and name the two flakes; the Oracle records it.


    ## Report from seat:01M7ZVK9YFPRSBR7EJF6DPC5E1

    Landed signed term commit 1e23b5207 on origin/main. make land exited 0 with 1,972 nextest passes across six packages. The fixes removed dependence on implicit JSON key order, the ACP error reply for token and round limits, and the invalid loader image comparison. The exact landed SHA still has a make test-parity exit of 2 for projection_ownership_real_io_survives_cancel_restart_and_root_aba (shutdown timing) and twenty_commit_rebase_keeps_control_requests_responsive (Git temporary-file EINVAL). Both passed serially and the Oracle assigned both to parallel-run-flakes. The harness pin is bd4893b3 and both worktrees are clean.

